  "card": "Validates outbound message types and payload sizes in CConnman::PushMessage() before queuing, asserting in debug builds and dropping oversized messages in release builds. Outbound transports assume a 12-byte message type and a 4 MB payload limit; exceeding them previously caused V1 encoding to abort, caused V2 encoding to write out of bounds or truncate types, and allowed sendmsgtopeer to send payloads that triggered peer disconnections. The sendmsgtopeer RPC now returns an RPC error when payloads exceed 4 MB. It has no PR dependencies.",
